From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:38:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: fix mt7996 RX NAPI teardown

mt76_dma_init() deliberately does not initialize some NAPI instances for
WED RRO queues, but mt76_dma_cleanup() tries to delete every RX NAPI
instance.  On MT7987 with MT7990 and WED 3.1 this reaches netif_napi_del()
with an uninitialized object and panics during mt7996e module removal.

The remaining mt7996 RX NAPI instances are still enabled when their page
pools are destroyed, which also triggers the page-pool race warning.

Nicolas Cavallari's upstream fix disabled every mt76 RX NAPI in the shared
cleanup path and skipped deletion based on the WED RRO queue role.  It was
reverted because mt7921 and mt7925 already disable their NAPI instances,
and a second napi_disable() can hang.

Use NAPI_STATE_LISTED as the authoritative initialized-state test in the
common deletion path.  Move the disable operation into
mt7996_dma_cleanup(), where the teardown path does not otherwise disable
these instances, and apply the same state test there.  Iterate the complete
NAPI array rather than mt76_for_each_q_rx(), since descriptor-less queues
can still own a registered NAPI instance.  This also handles a non-WED
mt7996 instance correctly instead of assuming that every queue with a WED
RRO role was left uninitialized.

Fixes: 7dd72bbd6f51 ("wifi: mt76: Fix memory leak destroying device")
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/332bbe9b2784bea2fd2b00fceb8eacf0fba06728
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/commit/6d1c6a758a4c0a690ee56cb849387dfa262fdb17
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 dma.c        | 6 +++++-
 mt7996/dma.c | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/dma.c
+++ b/dma.c
@@ -1218,7 +1218,11 @@ void mt76_dma_cleanup(struct mt76_dev *dev)
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dev->q_rx); i++) {
+		if (test_bit(NAPI_STATE_LISTED, &dev->napi[i].state))
+			netif_napi_del(&dev->napi[i]);
+	}
+
 	mt76_for_each_q_rx(dev, i) {
 		struct mt76_queue *q = &dev->q_rx[i];
 
-		netif_napi_del(&dev->napi[i]);
 		mt76_dma_rx_cleanup(dev, q);
 
 		page_pool_destroy(q->page_pool);
--- a/mt7996/dma.c
+++ b/mt7996/dma.c
@@ -1093,7 +1093,17 @@ void mt7996_dma_reset(struct mt7996_dev
 
 void mt7996_dma_cleanup(struct mt7996_dev *dev)
 {
+	int i;
+
 	mt7996_dma_disable(dev, true);
 
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dev->mt76.q_rx); i++) {
+		if (!test_bit(NAPI_STATE_LISTED,
+			      &dev->mt76.napi[i].state))
+			continue;
+
+		napi_disable(&dev->mt76.napi[i]);
+	}
+
 	mt76_dma_cleanup(&dev->mt76);
 }
